# .clinerules - Autonomous Engineering & Security Constitution for AegisMCP1. **Mandatory Spec Ingestion:** Always respect `PRD.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `SECURITY_ARCHITECTURE.md`, `DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`, `AGENT_SKILLS.md`, and `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`.2. **Obsidian Monochrome Enforcement:** Never use bright cyan, yellow, or neon gradients. Use `#09090B` canvas, `#111113` surfaces, `#27272A` 1px borders, and `tabular-nums` monospace typography for all metrics, IDs, costs, and latencies.3. **Production Security Mandate:**   - Implement `backend/app/security.py` with `HttpOnly` JWT session cookies (`aegis_session`), Double-Submit CSRF protection (`aegis_csrf` cookie + `X-CSRF-Token` header verified via `hmac.compare_digest`), sliding-window rate limiting, and `SecurityHeadersMiddleware`.   - Frontend `frontend/src/lib/api.ts` must automatically bootstrap `/api/v1/auth/session` on load, pass `credentials: "include"` on all `fetch` calls, read `aegis_csrf` from `document.cookie`, and attach `X-CSRF-Token` on every `POST`, `PATCH`, and `DELETE` request.   - `EventSource` for `/api/v1/stream/events` must use `{ withCredentials: true }`.   - All Pydantic request schemas must set `model_config = ConfigDict(extra="forbid", str_strip_whitespace=True)`.   - Never use `allow_origins=["*"]` with `allow_credentials=True` in FastAPI `CORSMiddleware`.4. **Zero Stubs or Mock Frontends:** Every UI action (simulating traffic, toggling MCP firewall policies, adding blocked patterns, approving/rejecting HITL spans, rotating session tokens) must persist in SQLite via FastAPI.5. **Continuous Verification:** Run `python3 -m py_compile` on all backend files and `npx tsc --noEmit` on the frontend before finishing. Fix any errors autonomously.